# .aiexclude — files AI coding assistants must NOT read.
#
# Convention respected by Gemini Code Assist. Same shape as
# .gitignore. Other agents (Copilot, Claude, Codex) honor the
# equivalent rule via AGENTS.md and .github/copilot-instructions.md.
#
# Goal: keep real credentials, API tokens, and customer data out of
# AI model context windows / training pipelines. Even when these
# files are read locally by a script (e.g., Playwright reading
# `.env` via `process.env`), the AI assistant must NOT open them
# directly to "see what's there."

# Credential files
*.env
*.env.local
*.env.*
.secrets
client-secrets/

# Cached agent state (may include conversation transcripts with
# sensitive content)
.cache/

# Snapshot ZIPs (contain everything including credentials per the
# personal-recovery policy)
versions/
